  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="b1f4743c-7a6e-5836-8701-f92a75694773" activityNameId="5a5e07b9-0eeb-5454-b051-895a6a99c653" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">xxx Butanol, 1-, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: xxx Butanol, 1-, at plant
The process considered is the production of 1-butanol by means of hydroformylation of propylene (oxo sinthesis). Manufacturing process starting with propylene is considered, plus consumption of energy, infrastructure and land use, as well as generation of solid wastes and emissions into air and water. Transport of the raw materials and solid wastes is included. No by-product is generated in the process. Transportation and consumption of auxiliaries are not included due to the lack of data. Transport and storage of the final product are not included. Transcient or unstable operations are not considered, but the production during stable operation conditions. Emissions to air are considered as emanating in a high population density area. Emissions into water are assumed to be emitted into rivers. Solid wastes are assumed to be sent to landfill. Inventory refers to 1 kg 100% 1-butanol. In the source used (von Däniken et al. 1995) numbers for emissions are taken from the manufacturing of acetic acid, as an approximation.;
CAS number: 000071-36-3; 
Formula: C4H10O; 
Synonyms: Butylalkohol; 
UUID: 3cdd8c25-34a5-3305-8b1f-058505becbac
production of 1-butanol by means of hydroformylation of propylene (oxo sinthesis)
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: unknown
Time period: literature bases on data from the 1990s.
Production volume: na
Sampling: see geography 
Extrapolations: Transports based on standard distances of Ecoinvent. Infrastructure: proxy module used (chemical plant, organics)
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_3cdd8c25-34a5-3305-8b1f-058505becbac.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
